1
00:00:11,640 --> 00:00:14,140
Let go of my hand this instant, sinner!

2
00:00:14,540 --> 00:00:17,080
I would rather die than be saved by you!

3
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:19,359
I will not bear the disgrace of it!

4
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:23,357
Hey! Stop!

5
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:24,277
Don't, you idiot!

6
00:00:24,360 --> 00:00:25,860
What's suicide gonna do?

7
00:00:26,120 --> 00:00:27,277
Nothing, that's what!

8
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:29,897
So suck it up, act like a
knight, and quit being an idiot!

9
00:00:29,980 --> 00:00:34,377
Idiot how dare you a
common criminal insult me i

10
00:00:34,460 --> 00:00:37,497
demand an apology oh shut
up i called you an idiot!

11
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:40,277
Because you're acting
like an idiot idiot listen

12
00:00:40,360 --> 00:00:43,717
if i let go when you die
then what eugio's still

13
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:46,017
in the cathedral and
he's on his way up to the

14
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:49,240
pontifex and it's your
job to stop him you idiot

15
00:00:51,220 --> 00:00:53,537
instead of checking
out an integrity knight

16
00:00:53,620 --> 00:00:56,397
should be thinking how to
get back in But not you!

17
00:00:56,480 --> 00:01:00,833
You're so dumb you forgot your priorities,
and that's why you're an idiot!

18
00:01:00,920 --> 00:01:01,780
Look here.

19
00:01:01,960 --> 00:01:05,254
I won't allow a rogue like
you to insult me any further.

20
00:01:07,340 --> 00:01:11,160
That said, your words have
a certain logic to them.

21
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:15,237
However, death is more tolerable
than being saved out of pity,

22
00:01:15,320 --> 00:01:17,737
and letting me fall
would benefit your cause.

23
00:01:17,820 --> 00:01:21,620
So why don't you explain why
I must accept this situation?

24
00:01:22,740 --> 00:01:23,620
I'll try.

25
00:02:17,920 --> 00:02:19,277
Thank

26
00:02:19,360 --> 00:02:26,360
you!

27
00:02:48,860 --> 00:02:49,690
HAAAAAAA!

28
00:02:59,760 --> 00:03:00,590
Eugeo and me,

29
00:03:00,800 --> 00:03:02,777
we didn't break in and get this far up the

30
00:03:02,860 --> 00:03:05,389
cathedral just to
destroy the Axiom Church.

31
00:03:05,960 --> 00:03:09,500
We know the Dark Territory is
gonna invade the Human Empire,

32
00:03:09,680 --> 00:03:11,915
and we want to protect it same as you.

33
00:03:16,760 --> 00:03:20,897
You're one of the most powerful
integrity knights around and if I let you

34
00:03:20,980 --> 00:03:27,017
die we lose a valuable ally we can't
afford that why should I believe you you

35
00:03:27,100 --> 00:03:30,937
violated the greatest taboo of all
spilling the blood of a fellow human and

36
00:03:31,020 --> 00:03:35,477
cutting them down that's true but the

37
00:03:35,560 --> 00:03:38,089
axiom church and the
taboo index are wrong.

38
00:03:38,960 --> 00:03:42,254
Eugeo and I had a good reason
to attack Raios and Umber.

39
00:03:42,720 --> 00:03:46,157
The law slid upper class nobles like
them to whatever they want to innocent?

40
00:03:46,240 --> 00:03:47,070
people.

41
00:03:47,153 --> 00:03:51,100
Those bastards were gonna rape Ronie
and Tiese and get away with it.

42
00:03:51,320 --> 00:03:52,849
Do you think that's right?

43
00:03:52,940 --> 00:03:54,320
Do you think that's

44
00:03:54,880 --> 00:03:55,710
fair?

45
00:03:55,793 --> 00:03:56,623
Well, is it?

46
00:03:57,260 --> 00:03:58,200
Answer me!

47
00:03:58,440 --> 00:03:59,280
Is it right?

48
00:04:01,800 --> 00:04:03,640
The law is the law.

49
00:04:04,320 --> 00:04:06,040
A crime is a crime.

50
00:04:06,660 --> 00:04:09,097
If the people are allowed to decide what

51
00:04:09,180 --> 00:04:11,657
is right and wrong
according to their needs,

52
00:04:11,740 --> 00:04:14,420
how will we maintain order in the land?

53
00:04:15,720 --> 00:04:18,717
Yeah, well, Administrator
came up with all the laws.

54
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:21,760
So who decides if she's right or wrong?

55
00:04:22,300 --> 00:04:23,140
Sure, God!

56
00:04:23,460 --> 00:04:24,820
If I'm such a sinner,

57
00:04:25,100 --> 00:04:28,217
then how come I haven't been fried
by a bolt of lightning by now?

58
00:04:28,300 --> 00:04:29,130
Simple.

59
00:04:29,520 --> 00:04:33,880
It is the will of Stacia, and
we knights enforce her will.

60
00:04:34,060 --> 00:04:35,557
We are her divine servants.

61
00:04:35,640 --> 00:04:39,993
All you knights in force are lies, and
me and Eugeo came here to prove it.

62
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:43,177
If we defeat Administrator,
we'll enter tyranny.

63
00:04:43,260 --> 00:04:44,800
We're not the bad guys.

64
00:04:45,280 --> 00:04:47,600
If we were, I'd have let you fall.

65
00:04:53,420 --> 00:04:54,700
It's coming loose!

66
00:04:54,980 --> 00:04:57,720
Stick your sword in the wall, or we die!

67
00:05:02,180 --> 00:05:03,597
What are you waiting for?

68
00:05:03,680 --> 00:05:04,510
Do it!

69
00:05:04,593 --> 00:05:06,340
Mine's about to come out! Hurry!

70
00:05:29,340 --> 00:05:31,520
I did not save you, sinner.

71
00:05:31,980 --> 00:05:33,627
I returned the favor is all.

72
00:05:35,020 --> 00:05:37,580
Besides, our duel has yet to be decided.

73
00:05:38,300 --> 00:05:39,460
If we survive.

74
00:05:40,040 --> 00:05:42,180
Oh well, at least we're even now.

75
00:05:44,180 --> 00:05:46,180
I got an idea if you want to hear.

76
00:05:47,360 --> 00:05:49,040
We can't hang here all day.

77
00:05:49,400 --> 00:05:53,812
Our arms will get tired, but if we work
together we can find a way back in.

78
00:05:53,900 --> 00:05:57,020
So like, what do you say
we call a truce till then?

79
00:05:57,400 --> 00:05:58,960
A truce? Yeah.

80
00:05:59,420 --> 00:06:01,637
We can't break the wall
so we'll have to climb.

81
00:06:01,720 --> 00:06:03,955
It'll be easier if we help each other.

82
00:06:04,440 --> 00:06:05,852
You say help each other.

83
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:07,980
How do you propose we do that?

84
00:06:08,260 --> 00:06:11,297
If one of us starts to fall, the
other stops them, that's all.

85
00:06:11,380 --> 00:06:14,237
If we had a rope, we could
use it as a safety line.

86
00:06:14,320 --> 00:06:15,908
I didn't bring one, though.

87
00:06:16,420 --> 00:06:20,620
I hate to admit it, but
that does sound logical.

88
00:06:21,920 --> 00:06:22,750
Very well.

89
00:06:25,180 --> 00:06:29,617
However, the moment we set foot
inside again, I will cut you down.

90
00:06:29,700 --> 00:06:30,880
True, sir, no.

91
00:06:31,280 --> 00:06:32,720
Do not forget that.

92
00:06:33,580 --> 00:06:34,840
I'll try not to.

93
00:06:35,380 --> 00:06:36,210
Now then.

94
00:06:36,293 --> 00:06:37,760
You said we needed rope.

95
00:06:38,780 --> 00:06:39,760
System call.

96
00:06:40,040 --> 00:06:40,940
Form object.

97
00:06:41,280 --> 00:06:42,120
Change shape.

98
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:49,100
W-was that the matter conversion art?

99
00:06:49,280 --> 00:06:51,240
Did you not hear what I said?

100
00:06:51,460 --> 00:06:53,560
I changed the shape of an object.

101
00:06:53,960 --> 00:06:58,117
Only the pontifex can use the formal
arts to change an object's properties,

102
00:06:58,200 --> 00:06:59,030
you dolt.

103
00:07:00,420 --> 00:07:01,340
Sorry, ma 'am.

104
00:07:26,760 --> 00:07:29,157
Hey, um, I just thought of something else.

105
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:30,080
What is it?

106
00:07:30,760 --> 00:07:32,740
It's about that dragon of yours.

107
00:07:33,080 --> 00:07:35,760
Can't you, like, summon it to come get us?

108
00:07:36,220 --> 00:07:40,380
Mine cannot fly further than the
landing platforms on the 30th floor.

109
00:07:40,700 --> 00:07:41,860
No dragon can.

110
00:07:42,140 --> 00:07:44,400
Even my uncle... Pardon.

111
00:07:44,720 --> 00:07:46,838
Even the commander's is not allowed.

112
00:07:47,520 --> 00:07:49,660
The upper floors are off-limits.

113
00:07:49,940 --> 00:07:51,411
Even the birds stay away.

114
00:07:52,260 --> 00:07:54,142
The Pontifex herself made it so.

115
00:07:54,640 --> 00:07:59,280
She cast a formal art, one so
advanced I do not even know it.

116
00:07:59,860 --> 00:08:00,690
Oh well.

117
00:08:01,280 --> 00:08:04,045
I guess that leaves us
with three options then.

118
00:08:04,360 --> 00:08:07,840
Go up or down, or bust
through the wall again.

119
00:08:08,260 --> 00:08:09,920
The third option is out.

120
00:08:10,360 --> 00:08:13,840
The cathedral walls are endowed
with nearly infinite life.

121
00:08:14,040 --> 00:08:17,700
And, as you saw, they
regenerate quickly. Perfect.

122
00:08:18,840 --> 00:08:21,075
Alright, I'm thinking we should climb.

123
00:08:21,360 --> 00:08:24,831
Do you know if there's anywhere
up top where we can get in?

124
00:08:25,840 --> 00:08:26,720
There is.

125
00:08:27,880 --> 00:08:30,680
The Morningstar lookout
is on the 95th floor.

126
00:08:31,120 --> 00:08:33,061
There are no walls, just pillars.

127
00:08:33,460 --> 00:08:36,840
If we can climb up that far,
we can easily get back in.

128
00:08:37,460 --> 00:08:38,320
That said,

129
00:08:38,780 --> 00:08:45,080
if we manage to survive the climb and get
in, our truce is off, and I will slay you.

130
00:08:45,280 --> 00:08:47,574
I know, I didn't forget about our deal.

131
00:08:48,800 --> 00:08:51,212
So are you okay with climbing up or what?

132
00:08:52,220 --> 00:08:53,050
Yes.

133
00:08:53,133 --> 00:08:57,604
Going up is more practical than down, but
how do you plan on scaling a sheer wall?

134
00:08:57,800 --> 00:08:59,040
It won't be easy.

135
00:09:00,160 --> 00:09:00,997
System call!

136
00:09:01,080 --> 00:09:03,520
Generate metallic element! Wedge shape!

137
00:09:17,620 --> 00:09:19,400
Is that safe to stand on?

138
00:09:20,400 --> 00:09:22,440
Seems to be, for now.

139
00:09:24,120 --> 00:09:24,950
System call.

140
00:09:25,240 --> 00:09:26,769
Generate metallic element.

141
00:09:32,220 --> 00:09:34,300
You know, I think this will work.

142
00:09:34,700 --> 00:09:36,580
Well, don't just hang there.

143
00:09:36,780 --> 00:09:37,620
Do what I did.

144
00:09:38,720 --> 00:09:39,740
I cannot.

145
00:09:41,340 --> 00:09:42,170
Huh?

146
00:09:42,253 --> 00:09:43,083
What do you mean?

147
00:09:43,240 --> 00:09:44,960
I said, I cannot.

148
00:09:45,380 --> 00:09:46,660
Yeah, I heard that.

149
00:09:46,880 --> 00:09:48,704
But what do you mean you can't?

150
00:09:49,400 --> 00:09:51,217
If I can make a wedge, you can.

151
00:09:51,300 --> 00:09:52,600
And you're so strong,

152
00:09:52,740 --> 00:09:55,757
you shouldn't have any problem
hoisting - That is not what I meant!

153
00:09:55,840 --> 00:09:59,720
I have never been in a situation
like this before today.

154
00:10:00,160 --> 00:10:05,500
At the risk of sounding weak, it is
all I can manage to just hang on.

155
00:10:05,760 --> 00:10:08,360
I cannot climb up onto
such a slender step.

156
00:10:08,920 --> 00:10:09,900
No worries.

157
00:10:10,180 --> 00:10:12,197
How about if I pull you up to the bar?

158
00:10:12,280 --> 00:10:14,162
Would that work for you instead?

159
00:10:14,380 --> 00:10:16,260
I would appreciate it.

160
00:10:16,560 --> 00:10:18,757
Okay, first I'm going
to take up the slack.

161
00:10:18,840 --> 00:10:19,857
here goes

162
00:10:19,940 --> 00:10:26,940
I'm

163
00:10:28,680 --> 00:10:29,510
ready go

164
00:10:29,593 --> 00:10:30,889
on and pull your sword out

165
00:10:52,140 --> 00:10:53,700
Grab the wall to balance.

166
00:10:56,260 --> 00:10:59,378
All right, I'm going to
climb up a little higher now.

167
00:10:59,680 --> 00:11:01,621
I'll let you know when I'm ready.

168
00:11:02,260 --> 00:11:04,360
Please be careful. Always.

169
00:11:27,100 --> 00:11:29,060
Hey, Asuna. Huh?

170
00:11:29,640 --> 00:11:30,581
How's your fish?

171
00:11:30,820 --> 00:11:33,996
I bet they caught it right
off the side of the turtle.

172
00:11:34,580 --> 00:11:36,040
Yeah, maybe they did.

173
00:11:36,980 --> 00:11:39,420
Or maybe they brought it. Who?

174
00:11:42,160 --> 00:11:42,990
Hmm.

175
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:44,270
I doubt it.

176
00:11:45,060 --> 00:11:47,001
Doesn't look like a fishing boat.

177
00:11:47,140 --> 00:11:49,020
It's got way too many antennas.

178
00:11:49,440 --> 00:11:50,580
Is it a battleship?

179
00:11:50,820 --> 00:11:52,160
No, it's Japanese.

180
00:11:52,720 --> 00:11:55,367
We don't have battleships
in service anymore.

181
00:11:55,860 --> 00:11:56,690
Ms.

182
00:11:56,773 --> 00:11:58,300
Yuki, Dr. Kojiro, morning.

183
00:11:58,860 --> 00:11:59,690
Good morning.

184
00:12:00,100 --> 00:12:01,780
Good morning, Mr. Nakanishi.

185
00:12:02,380 --> 00:12:05,080
If that's not a warship, is it SDF?

186
00:12:06,100 --> 00:12:06,930
MSDF.

187
00:12:07,013 --> 00:12:09,660
And Escort Ship is the
official designation.

188
00:12:10,380 --> 00:12:13,620
The one out there is the DD-119 Asahi.

189
00:12:13,880 --> 00:12:16,233
She's a five-ton general purpose vessel.

190
00:12:16,500 --> 00:12:18,920
She's one of two escort ships in service.

191
00:12:19,300 --> 00:12:21,077
Her sister's ship is the Shiranui.

192
00:12:21,160 --> 00:12:23,577
Hey, um, it looks like
it's moving away now.

193
00:12:23,660 --> 00:12:26,248
They are the second
generation of her class.

194
00:12:28,440 --> 00:12:29,280
Pardon me.

195
00:12:33,440 --> 00:12:38,300
Lieutenant Colonel Kikuoka, I just saw
the Asahi changing course to the west.

196
00:12:39,400 --> 00:12:43,341
Wasn't she supposed to stay with
us until 1200, day after tomorrow?

197
00:12:44,100 --> 00:12:45,580
Yes, sir. Right away.

198
00:12:47,880 --> 00:12:49,060
Excuse me, ladies.

199
00:12:49,300 --> 00:12:50,476
Something's come up.

200
00:12:54,720 --> 00:12:56,700
It must be something important.

201
00:12:58,600 --> 00:12:59,430
Yeah...

202
00:13:20,580 --> 00:13:21,620
System call.

203
00:13:22,020 --> 00:13:23,549
Generate Metallic Element.

204
00:13:24,420 --> 00:13:25,460
The light.

205
00:13:30,880 --> 00:13:35,000
Generating containers uses up a
significant amount of sacred power.

206
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:40,100
And once Solace sets, we'll be lucky
if we can create one bar an hour.

207
00:13:41,540 --> 00:13:43,660
How high up do you think we are now?

208
00:13:45,500 --> 00:13:48,700
Um, I think we're already
past the 85th floor.

209
00:13:49,140 --> 00:13:52,320
The 95th floor is still
quite a long way off.

210
00:13:53,480 --> 00:13:57,951
Yeah, and climbing's gonna be even more
dangerous once it's too dark to see.

211
00:14:00,560 --> 00:14:01,760
Hey, check it out!

212
00:14:01,940 --> 00:14:03,822
There's something on that ledge!

213
00:14:05,840 --> 00:14:09,400
They look like statues
from here, which is odd.

214
00:14:09,560 --> 00:14:10,777
No one below can see them.

215
00:14:10,860 --> 00:14:12,300
Oh, well, they're lost.

216
00:14:12,460 --> 00:14:14,217
But maybe we can rest on them.

217
00:14:14,300 --> 00:14:16,437
They look like they're about six meter...

218
00:14:16,520 --> 00:14:18,140
six miles away.

219
00:14:18,460 --> 00:14:20,284
We're gonna need two more bars.

220
00:14:20,860 --> 00:14:22,940
You only need two, Yusei?

221
00:14:24,420 --> 00:14:25,580
Very well, then.

222
00:14:26,160 --> 00:14:28,560
I was saving it for an emergency.

223
00:14:29,140 --> 00:14:31,220
It appears this would be one.

224
00:14:33,620 --> 00:14:34,617
Form object.

225
00:14:34,700 --> 00:14:35,580
Wedge shape.

226
00:14:38,120 --> 00:14:39,560
Here, use these.

227
00:14:40,560 --> 00:14:41,390
Thanks.

228
00:14:41,473 --> 00:14:42,460
I owe ya.

229
00:14:53,460 --> 00:14:54,640
Get ready.

230
00:14:54,820 --> 00:14:55,717
I'm pulling you up.

231
00:14:55,800 --> 00:14:56,630
Right.

232
00:14:58,560 --> 00:14:59,390
You good?

233
00:15:00,560 --> 00:15:01,390
I'm fine.

234
00:15:07,100 --> 00:15:07,930
No.

235
00:15:09,560 --> 00:15:10,680
Oh, my God.

236
00:15:11,080 --> 00:15:13,200
That sure is one ugly statue.

237
00:15:18,220 --> 00:15:20,340
It's from the Dark Territory!

238
00:15:24,540 --> 00:15:25,460
Alice!

239
00:15:28,440 --> 00:15:29,360
Alice!

240
00:15:51,780 --> 00:15:53,680
Draw your sword! Hurry!

241
00:15:53,960 --> 00:15:55,372
There's two more coming!

242
00:15:59,420 --> 00:16:00,250
Atlas!

243
00:16:05,340 --> 00:16:07,760
We're screwed if they attack at once.

244
00:16:08,660 --> 00:16:10,560
What the hell's up with her?

245
00:16:14,020 --> 00:16:14,850
Alice!

246
00:16:17,280 --> 00:16:18,110
Alice!

247
00:16:18,440 --> 00:16:20,280
Hang on as tight as you can!

248
00:16:20,900 --> 00:16:22,340
No, just a moment.

249
00:16:22,660 --> 00:16:25,160
I'll apologize later if we survive.

250
00:16:25,860 --> 00:16:26,690
Get ready!

251
00:16:27,720 --> 00:16:30,300
One, two, three!

252
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:54,000
What were you thinking, you idiot?

253
00:16:54,360 --> 00:16:55,780
Have you lost your mind?

254
00:16:56,460 --> 00:16:58,360
I didn't have any other choice.

255
00:16:58,660 --> 00:16:59,560
I had to act.

256
00:17:00,300 --> 00:17:01,400
We'll talk later.

257
00:17:01,600 --> 00:17:02,482
Here they come!

258
00:17:13,360 --> 00:17:14,840
There is no doubt.

259
00:17:17,420 --> 00:17:19,140
But why are they here?

260
00:17:19,440 --> 00:17:21,911
I was wondering when you'd snap out of it.

261
00:17:22,180 --> 00:17:24,217
Do you know what these monsters are?

262
00:17:24,300 --> 00:17:26,417
Yes, I do indeed.

263
00:17:26,500 --> 00:17:30,380
Indeed, they are familiars
from the Dark Territory,

264
00:17:30,700 --> 00:17:35,620
conjured from lumps of corrupt soil by
sorcerers who practice the dark arts.

265
00:17:36,400 --> 00:17:38,020
Such disgusting things.

266
00:17:38,660 --> 00:17:42,000
